Clear Array.find value ownership after release

quickjs-ng's own fix, upstream commit e22ce4de4362dc5fd4794cfa3c03fc7fdba5f015
"Clear Array.find value ownership after release (#1826)", by Qi Deng,
2026-11-02, on quickjs-ng master after v0.18.0 (MIT, as the engine is).
Rebased by line number onto the v0.18.0 release amalgamation that
contrib/quickjs/amalgamation.lock pins; the change itself is the upstream
one line.

js_array_find (behind find, findIndex, findLast and findLastIndex) released
the step's element at the end of each step without clearing `val`. When the
interrupt poll at the top of the next step stopped JavaScript (a deadline, a
cancel or a stop cell), the exception path released the previous element a
second time, which frees an object the array still points at.

Drop this file when the lock pins a quickjs-ng release that contains
e22ce4de43 (none did as of 2026-11-21; the latest release was v0.18.0).

--- a/quickjs-amalgam.c
+++ b/quickjs-amalgam.c
@@ -56505,6 +56505,7 @@
             }
         }
         JS_FreeValue(ctx, val);
+        val = JS_UNDEFINED;
         JS_FreeValue(ctx, index_val);
     }
     JS_FreeValue(ctx, obj);
